---
import Layout from "../../layouts/Layout.astro";
---

<Layout
  title="Miranda · About · UX & Product Consultant"
  description="UX & Product Consultant specialised in complex software, workflow design and operational processes. I work between business, users and development teams."
  page="about-en"
  bg='data-max="110" data-link="155" data-accent="0.08" data-speed="0.12"'
>
  <section class="page-hero">
    <div class="shell">
      <div class="hero-grid" style="align-items:center;">
        <div>
          <div class="eyebrow reveal">About</div>
          <h1 class="reveal d1">I look for the right problem before designing anything.</h1>
          <p class="lede reveal d2">I'm a UX &amp; Product Consultant. I work with companies and organisations that have complex processes and can't afford to get their digital decisions wrong. I don't sell a transformation story. I help you make a decision you can actually defend.</p>
          <div class="cta-row reveal d3"><a class="btn btn-primary btn-lg magnetic" href="https://calendly.com/mirandauxdesigner/30min" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><i data-lucide="calendar-check" class="ic"></i> Book a triage call</a></div>
        </div>
        <div class="reveal d2">
          <div class="holo glow-wine" style="padding:10px;aspect-ratio:4/5;">
            <img
              src="/assets/miranda-chisono.jpeg"
              alt="Miranda Giaccon, UX and Product Consultant"
              width="951"
              height="1280"
              fetchpriority="high"
              decoding="async"
              style="display:block;width:100%;height:100%;border-radius:14px;overflow:hidden;object-fit:cover;"
            />
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- WHAT I DO -->
  <section class="section tight">
    <div class="shell">
      <div class="section-head reveal"><div class="eyebrow">What I do</div><h2 class="h2-cinema">Multidisciplinary — looking at the whole picture.</h2><p>I hold together competencies that usually sit in separate rooms. It's in those gaps, in the handoffs between rooms, that digital projects tend to break.</p></div>
      <div class="offers grid-2cols reveal d1">
        <div class="card-d"><div class="ic-badge"><i data-lucide="compass"></i></div><h3 style="font-size:19px">UX &amp; Product Consulting</h3><p style="font-size:14px;line-height:21px;margin-top:8px;">From process mapping to product selection, through to long-term evolution. UX isn't just the interface, it's the decision behind it.</p></div>
        <div class="card-d"><div class="ic-badge"><i data-lucide="route"></i></div><h3 style="font-size:19px">Workflow &amp; Process Design</h3><p style="font-size:14px;line-height:21px;margin-top:8px;">I digitalise real processes, not imagined ones. First I understand how the work actually happens, then I select or change the tools.</p></div>
        <div class="card-d"><div class="ic-badge"><i data-lucide="git-branch"></i></div><h3 style="font-size:19px">Decision quality</h3><p style="font-size:14px;line-height:21px;margin-top:8px;">Shared criteria, explicit trade-offs, risks on the table. A decision that holds in a board meeting, not just in a workshop.</p></div>
        <div class="card-d"><div class="ic-badge"><i data-lucide="users-round"></i></div><h3 style="font-size:19px">Human-centred adoption</h3><p style="font-size:14px;line-height:21px;margin-top:8px;">Software only exists if people use it. I design adoption around the people who will work with it every day.</p></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- HOW I WORK -->
  <section class="section tight">
    <div class="shell">
      <div class="section-head reveal"><div class="eyebrow">How I work</div><h2 class="h2-cinema">Four things I genuinely care about.</h2></div>
      <div class="offers grid-4cols reveal d1">
        <div class="card-d"><h3 style="font-size:18px;color:var(--eyebrow-dark)">Rigour</h3><p style="font-size:14px;line-height:21px;margin-top:8px;">The small irritating details that seem minor are exactly what makes people abandon software.</p></div>
        <div class="card-d"><h3 style="font-size:18px;color:var(--eyebrow-dark)">Clarity</h3><p style="font-size:14px;line-height:21px;margin-top:8px;">Saying clearly what to do and what not to do, without hiding behind jargon.</p></div>
        <div class="card-d"><h3 style="font-size:18px;color:var(--eyebrow-dark)">Autonomy</h3><p style="font-size:14px;line-height:21px;margin-top:8px;">I leave you in a position to move forward independently, not dependent on me.</p></div>
        <div class="card-d"><h3 style="font-size:18px;color:var(--eyebrow-dark)">Sustainable pace</h3><p style="font-size:14px;line-height:21px;margin-top:8px;">We design transitions your team can actually manage, not sprints that burn people out.</p></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- BACKGROUND -->
  <section class="section tight">
    <div class="shell">
      <div class="holo reveal" style="padding:40px;">
        <div class="lead-2col" style="align-items:start;gap:48px;">
          <div>
            <div class="eyebrow">Background</div>
            <h2 class="h2-cinema" style="margin-top:14px;max-width:18ch;">From visual design to complex systems.</h2>
          </div>
          <div>
            <p style="font-size:15px;line-height:25px;color:var(--on-dark-2);margin:0 0 16px;">My background is multidisciplinary: visual design, UX, product strategy, process analysis. Over time I moved from designing screens to designing the systems behind them — understanding operational logic, translating it into functional requirements, and bridging the gap between what a business needs and what a development team can build.</p>
            <p style="font-size:15px;line-height:25px;color:var(--on-dark-2);margin:0;">Today I work mostly on complex B2B software: management systems, operational portals, data-driven workflows, internal tools. I sit between the client, the business, and the development team, keeping the quality of both the decision and the experience.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- WHAT I AM NOT -->
  <section class="section tight">
    <div class="shell">
      <div class="holo reveal" style="padding:40px;">
        <div class="lead-2col" style="align-items:center;">
          <div><div class="eyebrow">To avoid misunderstandings</div><h2 class="h2-cinema" style="margin-top:14px;max-width:14ch;">What I'm not.</h2></div>
          <ul style="list-style:none;margin:0;padding:0;display:grid;gap:12px;">
            <li style="display:flex;gap:11px;color:var(--on-dark-2);font-size:15px;"><i data-lucide="x" style="width:18px;color:#e89a9a;flex-shrink:0;margin-top:3px"></i> a web agency or software house</li>
            <li style="display:flex;gap:11px;color:var(--on-dark-2);font-size:15px;"><i data-lucide="x" style="width:18px;color:#e89a9a;flex-shrink:0;margin-top:3px"></i> a developer</li>
            <li style="display:flex;gap:11px;color:var(--on-dark-2);font-size:15px;"><i data-lucide="x" style="width:18px;color:#e89a9a;flex-shrink:0;margin-top:3px"></i> a course creator or trainer</li>
            <li style="display:flex;gap:11px;color:var(--on-dark-2);font-size:15px;"><i data-lucide="x" style="width:18px;color:#e89a9a;flex-shrink:0;margin-top:3px"></i> a decorative pixel-pusher</li>
            <li style="display:flex;gap:11px;color:var(--on-dark-2);font-size:15px;"><i data-lucide="x" style="width:18px;color:#e89a9a;flex-shrink:0;margin-top:3px"></i> a generic AI consultant</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- CTA -->
  <section class="section">
    <div class="shell">
      <div class="cta-band reveal">
        <div class="eyebrow center" style="justify-content:center;">Next step</div>
        <h2 style="margin-top:14px;">Tell me what the problem is.</h2>
        <p>If you're working on a complex digital product, an internal system or a process that's creating friction, a 30-minute triage call is the right starting point.</p>
        <div class="cta-row">
          <a class="btn btn-primary btn-lg magnetic" href="https://calendly.com/mirandauxdesigner/30min" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><i data-lucide="calendar-check" class="ic"></i> Book a triage call</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
